  "job_B3.3.28_20251003_114714": {
    "text": "Of Seinte Neote.\nM\u00e6n \u00fea leofeste, we wylle\u00f0 eow cy\u00f0en beo sumen d\u00e6le emb \u00feyssen halgen, \u00fee we tod\u00e6ig wur\u00f0ige\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t\nHit s\u00e6g\u00f0 on \u00fean halgen godspelle, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t liht on Godes gela\u00f0unge na behydd beon ne sceal, ac up asett\nSwa eac ne mihte Sanctus Neotus behydd beon ne bedigelod, \u00fea \u00fea God hine geupped habben wolde.\nHe w\u00e6s on iuge\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fee bec secge\u00f0, to boclicre lare gesett, & to godcunden \u00feeawen becom, & georne\nSwa hit awriten is, \u00fe\u00e6t se weig is sticol & neare, \u00fee to \u00fean ecen life belimp\u00f0, & nan mann \u00fe\u00e6r to ne\nSwa dyde Sanctus Neotus, forh\u00e6fde hine sylfne fram gelustfullunge \u00feysses lifes.\nHe w\u00e6s man\u00f0w\u00e6re & milde ealle mannen & he d\u00e6ighwamlice to his Drihtene clypode \u00e6fter Dauides\nDo beo me \u00e6fter \u00feinre mildheortnysse & t\u00e6c me \u00feine rihtwisnysse.\nSo\u00f0lice \u00fe\u00e6t ilca gebed us is alefd, gyf we wylle\u00f0 inweardlice to Gode clypigen & his mildheortnysse\nHit s\u00e6ig\u00f0 on gewritan, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fees halge were to Gl\u00e6stingebyrig gecerred w\u00e6re on Sanctes \u00e6lfeges dagen\n& his salmes & o\u00f0re gebedan he geornlice beeode d\u00e6iges & nihtes.\n& his gewune w\u00e6s, \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde on d\u00e6ig gelomen his cneowe gebegen, & eac swylce on niht to \u00fean\nHe gemunde symle his synnen, \u00fee he on his iuge\u00f0e gefremede, & \u00fea geornlice beweop & bereowsede,\nHe geneosode Romeburh seofe si\u00f0en Criste to lofe & Seinte Petre, & \u00fe\u00e6re his synnen forgyfenysse\nHe w\u00e6s on eallen Godes beboden swy\u00f0e fullfremed.\nSohte \u00fea weste stowe geond eall \u00feiss land on to wunigene, & \u00fea gemette he \u00feurh Godes foresceawunge.\nSeo is w\u00e6std\u00e6les \u00feysses landes, ten milen fram Petrocesstowe \u00fea me hatt Neotes stoca.\n& he him \u00fe\u00e6r wununge getimbrode on swy\u00f0e f\u00e6geren stowe, & myrige w\u00e6tersea\u00f0es \u00fe\u00e6r abuten\n\u00de\u00e6r se Godes \u00feeowe Sanctus Neotus his lif adreah on mycelre forh\u00e6fednysse, ofer m\u00e6n o\u00f0re modes &\nNe m\u00e6ig nan mann fullice gecy\u00f0en, hwu sti\u00f0lice he his lif adreah \u00e6r his m\u00e6ssepreosthade ne \u00e6fter.\nNe gl\u00e6ingde he his lichame mid deorewur\u00f0en scrude, ne he mid estmeten his inna\u00f0 ne gefyllde.\nMid \u00fean \u00fee he \u00feuss lange gedrohtned h\u00e6fde on \u00fe\u00e6re stowe, \u00fee we won \u00e6r fore s\u00e6den, \u00fea ongann se\nOngann \u00fea s\u00e6nden his \u00e6ttrige w\u00e6pnen, \u00fe\u00e6t synd costnungen, togeanes \u00fean halgen were.\nAc he \u00feone feond oferswa\u00f0 mid rihten geleafen \u00feurh Godes gescyldnysse.\nHim comen gelomen to halige Godes \u00e6ngles and hine gefrefreden & wel geherten, & hine manoden,\nHe dyde swa se \u00e6ngel bebead.\nBodede ealle mannen rihtne geleafe.\n\u00dean synfullen & \u00fean \u00fee heora synnen andetten wolden & \u00e6fre geswican, he behet Godes godnysse &\n& \u00fe\u00e6r toecan \u00fe\u00e6t ece lif, \u00fea gode he manode, \u00fe\u00e6t heo on heora godnysse \u00feurhwunedan.\nHit gelamp sume d\u00e6ige, \u00fe\u00e6t se halge were on \u00e6rnemorgen digellice ferde to his w\u00e6tersea\u00f0e, & \u00fe\u00e6r his\n\u00dea geherde he f\u00e6ringe ridenda menige.\nHe \u00fea hr\u00e6dlice mid mycelen ofste fram \u00fe\u00e6re welle onette, nolde \u00fe\u00e6t his drohtnung \u00e6nigen eor\u00f0lice\nForleas \u00fea on \u00fean f\u00e6relde his \u00e6nne scoh, & o\u00f0erne mid him to his gebedhuse ham gebrohte.\nMid \u00fean \u00fee he his salmes & his gebeden & r\u00e6dingan embhydiglice smeade, \u00fea becom him to gemynde\nClypode \u00fea him to his \u00feeign, & bebead him \u00fe\u00e6t he him his sco gefeccen scolde.\nHe \u00fea w\u00e6s his f\u00e6der bebodan gehersum, & hr\u00e6dlice ferde to \u00fe\u00e6re welle, & \u00fe\u00e6r on \u00fean wegge\n\u00de\u00e6t is \u00fe\u00e6t an fox, \u00fee is geapest ealra deora, \u00fe\u00e6r arn geond dunen & denen wunderlice beseonde mid\n\u00dea beseh \u00fe\u00e6r, to se arf\u00e6ste Drihten & nolde, \u00fe\u00e6t his \u00feeowe on swa medemlice \u00feingen geunrotsed\nGes\u00e6nde \u00fea sl\u00e6p on \u00feone fox, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he his lif alet, habbende \u00fea \u00fewanges of \u00fean sco on his fracede\nSe \u00feeign \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6r to geteignde & \u00feone sco genam & \u00fean halge gebrohte, & him cydde eall hw\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r\nHe \u00fea, se halge, \u00fe\u00e6s mycele wundrode, & bebead \u00fean \u00feeigne on \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes name, \u00fe\u00e6t he hit nanen\nOn \u00fean time w\u00e6s \u00e6lfred king, & to \u00fean halgen gelomen com emb his sawle \u00feearfe.\nHe hine eac \u00fereade manega worden & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0 mid forewitegunge, Eala, \u00feu king, mycel scealt \u00feu\nOn \u00fean towearden time, swa mycele angsumnysse \u00feu gebiden scealt, \u00fe\u00e6t nan m\u00e6nnisc tunge hit eall\nNu, leof bearn, geher me, gyf \u00feu wylt, & \u00feine heorte to mine r\u00e6de gecerre.\nGewit eallinge fram \u00feinre unrihtwisnysse, & \u00feine synnen mid \u00e6lmessen ales, & mid tearen adigole, &\nSe king \u00e6lfred dyde \u00fea swa se halge hine bebead, & his beboden georne hlyste, & he him feala\nSe halge eft cw\u00e6\u00f0 o\u00f0re wordan, Ic nylle \u00fee bedigeligen, gode king, \u00fe\u00e6t me toweard is forneh se d\u00e6ig\nAc ic secge get, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6fter minen for\u00f0si\u00f0e \u00feu feale \u00feoligen scealt, & fram Deniscre \u00feeode \u00feu aflemed\nSwa hit on Drihtenes \u00ferowunge awriten is \u00fe\u00e6t, \u00feone se herde aflemed & ofslagen by\u00f0, \u00feonne by\u00f0 \u00fea\nAc \u00feonne \u00fee ealre angsumest by\u00f0 on \u00feine mode, ge\u00f0\u00e6nc \u00feu min, & ic \u00fee gescilde on Drihtenes name.\n\u00dea se king \u00feas word geherde, \u00fea forhtode he \u00feearle swy\u00f0e, & his bletsunge ab\u00e6d, & aweig gewende.\nHim aneode sy\u00f0\u00f0en swa Sanctus Neotus him fores\u00e6de.\n\u00d0\u00e6s halgen untrumnysse weox \u00fea fram d\u00e6ge to d\u00e6ige, & \u00fea on \u00fean ytemesten d\u00e6ige his handbreden\nSo\u00f0lice engles togeanes his sawle comen, & heo gel\u00e6dden mid mycelen gefean to heofonrices\nHis leorningcnihtes \u00fea bebyrigden his lic mid mycelen wur\u00f0mynte innen \u00fe\u00e6re cirice, \u00fee he sylf on \u00e6r\n\u00de\u00e6r becom \u00fea on \u00fe\u00e6re hwile mycel swetnysse st\u00e6nc, swylc hit eall gestreawod w\u00e6re on \u00fe\u00e6re stowe\n& eft binnen seofen gearen his ban up genumen wur\u00f0en & on o\u00f0re stowe mid wurdmynte aleigd, neh\nHw\u00e6t, \u00fea word ealle gefyllede beon scolden, \u00fee se halge fores\u00e6de beo \u00fean kinge.\nCom \u00fea Gu\u00f0rum, se h\u00e6\u00f0ene king, mid his w\u00e6lreowen here \u00e6rest on eastd\u00e6le Sexlandes, & \u00fe\u00e6r feala\nSume eac fleames cepten, & sume on hand eodan.\n\u00dea \u00e6lfred king, \u00fee we \u00e6r embe sp\u00e6con, \u00fe\u00e6t ofaxode, \u00fe\u00e6t se here swa sti\u00f0lic w\u00e6s, & swa neh\nFerde \u00fea lutigende geond heges & weges, geond wudes & feldes, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00feurh Godes wissunge\nHit gelamp sume d\u00e6ige, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6s swanes wif h\u00e6tte hire ofen, & se king \u00fe\u00e6rbig s\u00e6t hleowwinde hine\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t yfele wif f\u00e6ringe astyrod, & cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00fean kinge eorre mode, W\u00e6nd \u00feu \u00fea hlafes, \u00fe\u00e6t\nHe w\u00e6s sone gehersum \u00fean yfele wife, for \u00fean \u00fee he nede scolde.\nHe \u00fea, se gode king, mid mycelre angsumnysse & siccetunge to his Drihtene clypode, his mildse\nHw\u00e6t, \u00fea abuten him aneode ealswa se halge him fores\u00e6de on \u00e6r, & mare eorfo\u00f0e he adreah, \u00feone we\nHe com to him anes nihtes on swefne swy\u00f0e brihte scinende, & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0, Eala, \u00feu king, hw\u00e6t\nHe wear\u00f0 afyrht on swefne f\u00e6rlice swy\u00f0e, & \u00feeh \u00fean halgen geandswerode, Eala, leof, he cw\u00e6\u00f0,\nIc eam ealles godes ben\u00e6med & mines kynerices.\nSe halge him andswerode, Ic eam Neotus, \u00fein freond, & ic nu blissige mid heofene Kinge.\nGehyht nu on his mihte, \u00feonne becumst \u00feu \u00e6fter Eastern to \u00feinen \u00e6\u00f0ele, & \u00fee togeanes cum\u00f0 \u00fein\nIc \u00fee toforen fare, \u00feu me \u00e6fterfolge, & \u00fein folc samod.\nIc so\u00f0lice todr\u00e6fe ealle \u00feine wi\u00f0erwinnen, & \u00feone king, \u00fee \u00fee togeanes win\u00f0, to geleafen gebege.\nHit gelamp \u00fea eall swa, & Gu\u00f0rum se h\u00e6\u00f0ene king com to \u00e6lfrede \u00fean cristene kinge, mid \u00fereottene\n& he twelf dages \u00e6fter \u00fean her on lande wunede mid mycelre blisse, & sy\u00f0\u00f0en gesund gewende mid\n\u00dea weox \u00e6lfredes cynerice, & his word wide sprang, \u00fe\u00e6t he on godcunden gewriten wel gel\u00e6red w\u00e6s,\nEac is to wytene, \u00fe\u00e6t se king \u00c6lfred manega bec \u00feurh Godes gast gedyhte.\n& binnen twam & twentig gearen his cynerices \u00feiss eor\u00f0lice lif forlet, & to \u00fean ecen gewende, swa\nEala, m\u00e6n \u00fea leofe, \u00fea w\u00e6ron gode dages on \u00fean gode time for cristenes folcas geearnunge, &\nNu is \u00e6ighwanen heof & wop, & orefcwealm mycel for folces synnen.\n& w\u00e6stmes, \u00e6ig\u00f0er gea on wude gea on felde, ne synd swa gode, swa heo iu w\u00e6ron, ac yfele\u00f0 swy\u00f0e\n& se \u00feinc\u00f0 nu w\u00e6rrest & geapest, \u00fee o\u00f0erne m\u00e6ig beswican, & his \u00e6hte him of anymen.\nEac man swere\u00f0 man mare \u00feone he scolde, \u00fey hit is \u00fee wyrse wide on eor\u00f0e, & beo \u00fean we mugen\nNe spare\u00f0 nu se f\u00e6der \u00fean sune, ne nan mann o\u00f0ren, ac \u00e6lc man win\u00f0 ongean o\u00f0ren, & Godes lage ne\nBeo \u00fean we mugen ongyten, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feiss wurld is aweigweard & swy\u00f0e neh \u00fean \u00e6nde \u00feysser wurlde.\nEale, ges\u00e6lig by\u00f0 se \u00fee hine sylfen on time gebyrege\u00f0.\nUten nu bidden georne Seinte Neoten & o\u00f0re halgen, \u00fe\u00e6t heo ure \u00feingeres beon to \u00fean Heofonkinge,",
